@! REGRESSION FIXTURE 2 of 2 - "full curve" = the full ride-through curve encoded into the
@! Option-3 CONs, as the app has generated it since 2026-09-24. ERCOT (NOGRR282) preset,
@! IT/UPS block, otherwise IDENTICAL to ercot_nogrr282_vendor_default_stages.dyr - only VDPA1-3/DMA1-3
@! (undervoltage) and VDUA1-3/TDUA1-3 (overvoltage) differ. Undervoltage stages reproduce
@! ERCOT Table A's own 4 mandatory rows exactly (0.90/2.00, 0.80/0.50, 0.50/0.25, 0.20/0.15).
@! Overvoltage stages 2-4 are set equal to the real single tier (1.20 pu / 2.00 s) instead
@! of the vendor-sample 1.2 pu / 0.0 s sentinel, so they can never trip earlier than intended.
@!
@! PSS/E v35.6.4 result: the two files behave DIFFERENTLY - the
@! vendor-default-stages file trips on a 1.25 pu / 0.1 s swell that this file rides through - which
@! proved Option 3's stages are live (see docs/developer/PERC1_MODEL.md "Option 3 is always live").
@! Note: this file preserves the encoding that was validated then; the app's current preset
@! export has since moved overvoltage stage 1 to the continuous ceiling, so it is not a
@! byte-for-byte copy of today's export.
@! Load ID fixed to '1' 2026-09-24 (was 'IT1', a 3-character id PSS/E's real
@! Load/USRLOD identifier field rejects).
@! ibus  LID  IT
100001 'USRLOD' '1' 'PERCBL' 12 1 2 173 33 250 0
@! ICON(M) ICON(M+1)  [ICON(M)=0 for 60 Hz, 1 for 50 Hz; ICON(M+1)=1 enables momentary
@! cessation (Option 2) in place of the undervoltage cease/reconnect (Option 1) used below]
 0 0
